# serializer version: 1
# name: test_feature_publish_mode_golden
  '''
  steps:
    - id: worktree
      activity: create-worktree
      input:
        agentId: "claude-agent"
        branch: "feature/{{params.slug}}"
    - id: setup
      activity: setup
      input:
        agentId: "claude-agent"
        setup:
          - cmd: "mkdir -p ~/.claude/skills && cp -r $H_SKILLS_DIR/. ~/.claude/skills/"
          - cmd: "cp $AGENT_APP_DIR/steering/h-lab-runtime.md ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md"
    - id: plan
      activity: run-claude
      input:
        cwd: "{{worktree.worktreePath}}"
        model: "claude-sonnet-4-6"
        permissionMode: plan
        task: |-
          You are in a git worktree of the target repository, on branch feature/{{params.slug}}.
  
          First check for a persisted plan from a prior run: if plan-feature-{{params.slug}}.md
          exists in the worktree root, read it — if it still matches the spec and the code,
          reuse it as your plan instead of re-investigating.
  
          Otherwise investigate the feature request under ===FEATURE SPEC=== below: explore the
          relevant code and produce an implementation plan. Do NOT write code or modify any
          files. If the feature already appears implemented, say so in the plan.
          End your response with the plan under the exact marker ===IMPLEMENTATION PLAN===.
  
          ===FEATURE SPEC===
          {{params.spec}}
    - id: implement
      activity: run-claude
      input:
        cwd: "{{worktree.worktreePath}}"
        model: "claude-haiku-4-5"
        task: |-
          You are in a git worktree of the target repository, on branch feature/{{params.slug}}.
  
          First persist the plan you were handed under ===IMPLEMENTATION PLAN=== (the
          shared-context handoff, so a re-run or another session can pick it up — the planning
          agent runs read-only and cannot write it itself):
          1. Write it to plan-feature-{{params.slug}}.md in the worktree root.
          2. Call the dapr MCP tool actor_state_set with actorId 'feature-{{params.slug}}' and key
             'plan', value the plan text — durable in the state store, inspectable from any
             session via actor_state_get.
          If either persistence step fails (e.g. the dapr MCP is unreachable), do NOT fail the
          run — but you MUST say so explicitly in your final output, so the degradation is
          visible instead of silent.
  
          Then implement the feature described under ===FEATURE SPEC=== below, following the
          plan. If the feature already appears implemented, make no changes and say so.
          Leave the result as working-tree changes while you work; whether the run ends
          committed, pushed, and opened as a PR is decided under ===CREATE PR=== below.
  
          ===CREATE PR===
          {{params.createPr}}
  
          ===ISSUE===
          {{params.issueNumber}}
  
          The value under ===CREATE PR=== above decides how this run ends. If it is not
          exactly 'true', leave everything as uncommitted working-tree changes — do not
          commit or push. If it IS 'true':
          1. Commit all working-tree changes on branch feature/{{params.slug}} with a concise
             conventional commit message.
          2. Push the branch. The origin remote has no credentials — derive <owner>/<repo>
             from `git remote get-url origin` and push with a one-shot token URL:
             git push "https://x-access-token:${GH_TOKEN}@github.com/<owner>/<repo>.git" feature/{{params.slug}}
             Never write the token into git config or the remote URL; if GH_TOKEN is unset,
             skip the push and say so under ===PR===.
          3. Open a pull request against the repository's default branch with the github
             MCP tool create_pull_request: title from the feature, body summarizing the
             spec, the plan, and what you implemented. If the value under ===ISSUE===
             above is a number N, include the line `Closes #N` on its own line in the PR
             body, so the merge auto-closes that issue. If a PR for this branch already
             exists, your push has updated it — do not open a duplicate.
          End your response with the exact marker ===PR=== on its own line, then the PR
          URL — or SKIPPED and the reason — on the next line.
  
          ===FEATURE SPEC===
          {{params.spec}}
  
          ===IMPLEMENTATION PLAN===
          {{plan.output}}
  
  '''
# ---
